The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) released its latest report in December 2018, which states that climate change is “the greatest challenge humanity faces.” It also says that there are many ways to reduce emissions of greenhouse gases, including reducing energy consumption, increasing efficiency, and using renewable energy sources such as solar power.
In addition, the IPCC says that the most effective way to tackle climate change is through policies that promote sustainable development. These include:
- Reducing carbon dioxide emissions from fossil fuels;
- Increasing energy efficiency;
- Promoting clean energy technologies;
- Creating jobs;
- Strengthening institutions and systems;
- Improving governance and accountability;
- Enhancing public health and well being;
- Ensuring access to affordable, reliable, sustainable, and modern energy services;
